      "content": "hey i been noticing some weird stuff with my smart trainers. like i feel like they’re picking up way more than just steps... almost like they’re tracking my rhythm or something. is there any actual proof that companies like nike or whatever are using the built in tech to profile people's biometric data for more than just fitness tracking? like for psychological stuff?",
